          "text": "SHAO I-ch'ên 邵懿辰 (T. 位西, H. 蕙西), 1810–1861, Dec. 31, scholar and bibliophile, who died a martyr in the Taiping rebellion, was a native of Jên-ho (Hangchow). Made a chü-jên in 1831, he obtained a post as a secretary of the Grand Secretariat (1841).",
